---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="About">
  <section class="section">
    <h1>About Pip and Kip</h1>
    <p>
      This Astro setup is intentionally lightweight: shared layout, reusable
      sections, and clear places for external data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Etsy and headless CMS integration can be handled through server-side
      endpoints, then rendered into existing cards and hero modules without
      changing page structure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="columns" aria-label="About columns">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Current Stack</h3>
      <p>
        Astro pages and static components for performance and maintainability.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Near-Term Plan</h3>
      <p>
        Add API adapters in <code>src/lib</code> and fetch data in pages or endpoints.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Scale Path</h3>
      <p>
        Promote reusable sections into CMS-configured blocks with typed
        contracts.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
